@startuml request-exact
' An exactly addressed request (docs/spec/03-transactions.md, section 3.1). The master frame and the slave frame
' are shortened to two bits each. The first response bit is low for every slave frame (type codes start with 1).
scale 10 as 70 pixels
hide time-axis
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
concise "Phase" as P
concise "DATA driven by" as D

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
P is idle
D is {-}
@10
CLK is high
P is START
D is master
@15
DATA is low
@20
CLK is low
P is "master frame: header, payload, CRC8"
@23
DATA is high
@30
CLK is high
@40
CLK is low
@43
DATA is low
@50
CLK is high
@60
CLK is low
P is "T"
D is nobody
@63
DATA is high
@70
CLK is high
@80
CLK is low
P is "slave frame: header, payload, CRC8"
D is "addressed slave"
@83
DATA is low
@100
CLK is high
@110
CLK is low
@113
DATA is high
@120
CLK is high
@130
CLK is low
P is STOP
D is master
@132
DATA is low
@140
CLK is high
@145
DATA is high
@150
CLK is low
P is idle
D is {-}
@160
P is {-}

CLK@80 <-> @100 : T_TURNAROUND
highlight 100 to 101 #Gold : first bit low = response
@enduml
